  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 1220 PM MDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nPWATs will continue to climb from Monday through Thursday, \nchallenging daily record values as the upper high sets up over \nTN/AL/MS and troughing along the west coast allows for a Monsoon \nmoisture plume to stand up over the region. This will be an \nincreasingly wet period, with daytime temps trending down, PoPs \ntrending up and an increasing threat for locally heavy rainfall \nand localized flash flooding. The threat for burn scar flash \nflooding will increase as well and be elevated all week. An upper \nlow/trough will move east toward the central Rockies Thursday and \nbring added forcing to the region, potentially enhancing\nconvection and the flash flood threat. The 12Z medium range model\nsolutions show a drop-off in PWATs beginning Friday and continuing\nthrough the weekend as an upper level ridge builds over the \nDesert SW and southern Great Basin, bringing a downtrend in PoPs.",
